From a111c6ae2015b36084a060f50ca8c9cff2fddf54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marnick Vandecauter <security@marnick.net>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 22:23:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] F22 + F20 + F33-F36: wrap submitter network I/O and add
 timeouts

Six telemetry-submitter blocks (FUNcube, PW-Sat2 authenticate, PW-Sat2
putPacket, BME authenticate, BME putPacket, BME WebSocket, SatNOGS DB
submit) wrapped their network calls without try/except inside a GR
basic_block.handle_msg. GR's thread-per-block scheduler catches uncaught
exceptions only at the very top of the thread function and never
respawns the thread, so any transient DNS / TCP RST / TLS / JSON parse
failure silently killed the block. The flowgraph kept accepting messages
into a queue that was no longer being drained.

Each call now wraps the request body in try/except, parses the response
body inside its own try/except, and uses timeout=10 to bound the I/O.

Reference: audit findings F22a/b/c, F20, F33, F34, F35, F36
CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H = 7.5
(AC downgraded from H to L: the BME warehouse path self-triggers on
every flowgraph start because gnd.bme.hu:8080 completes the TLS
handshake then closes the stream on anonymous connections. No
attacker required.)
